# Orfis feedback routing for DEVELOPMENT only — `tauri dev`, `pnpm dev`,
# `pnpm dev:mock`. Vite loads this file in `development` mode and never in a
# build, so a dev session cannot post into production by accident. That is the
# entire reason this exists as a second file rather than one shared `.env`.
#
# The laptop key's allowed origins are `http://localhost:1420` and
# `tauri://localhost`. Measured 2026-10-07 against the running dev API: a
# preflight to /v1/feedback echoes whichever Origin it is sent, and the per-key
# origin is enforced on the POST — so both of ours work. (Note the `tauri://`
# one is moot here: a packaged build loads .env.production, and this file's
# http endpoint is refused in a release build by design, below.)
#
# Fail-safe by construction, and verified against the real validator rather
# than assumed: `feedbackConfig` allows an http:// endpoint ONLY when the host
# is loopback AND `import.meta.env.DEV`. So this file reaching a release build
# is REFUSED outright — the laptop key cannot ship even by accident.
#
# The endpoint is a laptop API that is not running by default. Start it in the
# Orfis checkout: `pnpm dev:infra` + `pnpm dev:api`.
VITE_ORFIS_KEY=pk_worktrees_a4882c82f027766b48
VITE_ORFIS_API_URL=http://localhost:4100
